% =============================================================================
% references.bib: bibliography database (set up in preamble/references.tex).
%
% HOW THIS FILE WORKS
% - Each entry is @type{key, field = {value}, ...}. Cite it in the text with \cite{key}.
% - Keys follow  firstauthorsurname + year + first title word  (all lower case), e.g. kumar2018rev2.
% - Entries are in alphabetical order of key.
% - Write authors as "Surname, Given Names" joined by "and". biblatex-ieee abbreviates given names to initials and switches to "et al." itself.
% - Titles keep the capitalisation of the source; wrap acronyms and proper nouns in braces ({REV2}, {MCP}) so no style can ever lower-case them.
% - date = {YYYY-MM} or {YYYY}. eid = article number ("Art. no." in IEEE).
% - arXiv preprints are @misc with eprinttype = {arxiv}; they print as "arXiv:2508.20829 [cs.LG]".
% =============================================================================

